  {
    "id": "c002",
    "name": "Paragraph 1 — Definition of \"Material\" (2003 MTA)",
    "text": "1. The biological material to be provided to Recipient Scientist is the anti-CD19-BB-.; chirnerio T-eell receptor construct, Including any progeny, portions, unmodified derivatives and any accompanying know-how or data ('Material\"). Legal title to the Material shall remain with St. Jude. The Recipient acknowledges that the Material is or maybe the subject of a patent application. Except as provided in this Agreement, no express or implied licenses or other rights are provided to the Recipient under any patents, patent applications, trade secrets or other proprie tary rights of St. Jude, including any altered forms of the Material made by St. Jude."
  },
  {
    "id": "c003",
    "name": "2. Restriction on Use and Transfer",
    "text": "The Material is for use by Recipient Scientist or persone dIrectly supervised by Recipient Scientist. The Material may net be transferred or taken to any ether laboratory or made available to any other person or third party, but is to remain under the immediate and direct control of Redplent Scientist."
  },
  {
    "id": "c004",
    "name": "Paragraph 3 — Permitted use of Material (2003 MTA)",
    "text": "3. Recipient Scientist agrees that the Material will only be used to create a lentiviral chimeric, T-cell receptor construct to be used in pre-clinical studies."
  },
  {
    "id": "c005",
    "name": "4. No Human or Commercial Use",
    "text": "The Material may not be used in humans and will be stored, used, and disposed of in accordance with applicable law and regulations, The Material will not be used for any commercial purpose."
  },
  {
    "id": "c006",
    "name": "5. St. Jude's Right to Distribute",
    "text": "St. Jude retains the unresteicted rig ht to distribute the Material to other commercial or noncommercial entities."
